WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.130
"Marley was dead: to begin with."

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Christmas Eve.

3
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.650
A cold old man counts his money.

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.840
The clock runs through the night.

5
00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.280
Five blocks drop in: Stave 1 to Stave 5.

6
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.530
By Christmas morning, the same man glows.

7
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.090
A lifetime of meanness,
undone in one night.

8
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.240
How?

9
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.870
In this mission, you'll find out why
Dickens calls his chapters staves.

10
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.810
A stave is a verse of a song,
and this book is a carol.

11
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.090
It's a novella, published
on 19 December 1843.

12
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.780
Three spirits take Scrooge through
past, present and future, in order.

13
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:42.070
And you'll follow the clock, bell by bell,

14
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.770
through a single night.

15
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.920
Your mission: explain how Scrooge's
whole life changes in a single night.
